<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 10 December, from 1520 to 1948.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">Human Rights Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Observed on the anniversary of the UN General Assembly's adoption of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights in 1948, Human Rights Day reaffirms the inalienable rights and fundamental freedoms to which every person on Earth is entitled.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1520">1520 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">506 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Luther burns the papal bull against him</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittenberg">Wittenberg</a>'s Elster Gate, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> burned Leo X's bull threatening him with excommunication, along with books of canon law. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> excommunicated him the following month.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mississippi-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1817">1817 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">209 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mississippi becomes the 20th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> was admitted to the Union. Its fertile lands became the heart of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> economy built on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, and later a key battleground of the civil rights movement.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1869">1869 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">157 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wyoming Territory gives women the vote</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Governor John Campbell signed a law granting women in Wyoming Territory the right to vote and hold office, the first such law in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. Wyoming is still called the 'Equality State'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1896">1896 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">130 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alfred Nobel dies in San Remo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-nobel">Alfred Nobel</a>, the Swedish chemist who invented dynamite, died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. His will left most of his fortune to fund prizes, first awarded on the anniversary of his death in 1901.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1948">1948 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">78 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The UN adopts the Universal Declaration of Human Rights</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Meeting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, the UN General Assembly adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/universal-declaration-of-human-rights">Universal Declaration of Human Rights</a> without a vote against. The drafting committee was chaired by Eleanor Roosevelt.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
